&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping new opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Scoping new bets through market sizing, commercial modelling, partnerships evaluation, and budget/forecast analysis&lt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customers and users across the globe use Planet&#39;s data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Reliability Engineer with focus on Identity and Access Management (IAM) to join the Corporate Engineering team. As an SRE together with other engineers you will be responsible for the continuous operation, further development and enhancement of Planet’s corporate infrastructure and applications, acting as the technical authority for our enterprise identity ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, hybrid role which will require you to work from our Berlin, Haarlem or Ljubljana office 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact You’ll Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to ensure the operation of Planet’s internal IT systems, specifically architecting and maintaining our identity providers (Okta, Auth0, Keycloak).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing and create new solutions by engineering automated zero-day Joiner, Mover, and Leaver (JML) workflows directly from our HRIS (e.g., HiBob).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting &amp;amp; Tooling: Use Python or Go to automate repetitive tasks, build custom provisioning connectors for legacy applications, and enforce identity data minimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and reduce operational toil through automation, making our systems self-healing and predictable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Leverage APIs, Terraform, Ansible, or SaltStack to manage configurations as code, moving away from manual UI/CLI changes across our identity platforms.

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None; supervision of students and interns&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the simulation and model-learning engine at the centre of Constructor&#39;s quantum software. The work is numerics-heavy: differentiable simulation of physical systems, inference of model parameters from experimental data, and optimisation at scale. The role sits between physics and engineering and requires genuine depth in both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Simulation Engine&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain high-performance simulation code for open and closed quantum systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the differentiable simulation and automatic differentiation layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive performance. This code runs inside optimisation loops and speed decides what is possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and extend the Julia core and its Python interface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: simulation accuracy against measurement, runtime performance, API stability.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Model Learning and Optimisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement parameter inference and model learning from experimental data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on neural-network approaches to PDE solving and equation discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark against established academic tools and publish the comparison.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: benchmark results, methods adopted by the research group, publications.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 Research Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Constructor University faculty on joint research and grant applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise graduate students and interns working on the engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to course material on numerical simulation and machine learning for physics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: research collaborations initiated and sustained; students productive.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD or equivalent in physics, applied mathematics or computational science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scientific computing in Julia, Python, JAX or comparable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real numerical depth: ODE solvers, optimisation, stochastic processes, automatic differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published work, or code that others rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the interface layer for a scientific platform used by research teams to run complex physical experiments. The work is heavier than typical product frontend — live experiment monitoring, workflow graphs, large result sets, and users who are physicists rather than consumers. The Senior Frontend Engineer owns that layer end to end and sets the standard for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Frontend Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture, code and standards for the platform frontend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain complex interactive visualisation: directed workflow graphs, live monitoring, large-scale result inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle long-running asynchronous work properly — progress, failure states, partial results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the migration to the Constructor React component library.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: interface stability, adoption by the research team, migration delivered.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Quality and Practice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring test coverage and review discipline to a codebase built at research pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish component standards and a shared design language with the wider Constructor frontend group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reach into the backend when that is what unblocks the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: test coverage, defects reaching users, review turnaround.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 Working with Scientists&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with the physicists who use the interface. Understand the experiment, not just the ticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn vague scientific requirements into concrete interface decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: researchers able to run and monitor experiments without asking for help.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years frontend engineering with strong React. We will also talk to you if your recent work has been Svelte, Vue or Angular.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data visualisation beyond charting libraries — D3, custom SVG, graph layout algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TypeScript at production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable writing backend code in Python or similar when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Decathlon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decathlon aims to become the best sports digital platform and open ecosystem in the world. We want to enable customers to experience Decathlon through many local sport-centric experiences by connecting many third-party actors and services, in a secure and performant way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our digital teams in Lille, Paris (and more…) which bring together more than 5000 collaborators are united to build and scale digital products with the aim to always deliver the best value to our users. With a presence in more than 70 countries, Decathlon is committed to innovation, sustainability, and customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our PRISM (Supply Chain) is looking for an AI Engineer based in Paris. As an AI Engineer dedicated to agent deployment, you will be at the heart of a tight-knit technical team. Your will play a critical role in the industrialization, deployment and monitoring of our Agent capabilities. You will closely work with digital teams (Data, Product, Engineering) to architect the deployment infrastructure, design intelligence routing, and build secure infrastructure allowing our agents to interact natively with our corporate data and legacy systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy solid foundations that will allow our AI agents to be hosted, run, and interact smoothly with our systems during production release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design robust pipelines enabling multi-step asynchronous agentic execution (e.g., transactional ingestion and writing flows), by implementing distributed resilience patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate agentic orchestration SDKs (notably Google Vertex AI Agent SDK / ADK), bypassing &quot;black box&quot; limitations of managed frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficiently orchestrate agents in production while ensuring proper information processing, routing to the most suitable models, and guaranteeing optimal cost and token usage management. Also ensure quality and speed of task execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strictly define the scope of action for each agent. You guarantee they only access data and actions for which they are formally authorized, respecting our confidentiality rules, while ensuring data security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build advanced performance measurement and tracking pipelines to trace agent reflections and decisions from end to end in order to debug logic in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the team to define relevant and consistent data evaluation metrics relative to the defined functional specificities and metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hard Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust backend design (Python), operational mastery of containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and pipelines (CI/CD, automated testin

&lt;h4&gt;Why Kimchi?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great models are raw ingredients. Kimchi is what happens when you ferment them with good engineering. We started inside CAST AI helping companies run LLMs on their own Kubernetes clusters; today we run our own coding harness on any model you pick, and we run the models underneath it ourselves.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimchi Inference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One API line and a customer&#39;s existing client just works: DeepSeek, GLM, Kimi, MiniMax, Nemotron served serverless from our own GPU fleet (OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible, pay per token, spend visible per user, team, and key). When control matters, the same models run on the customer&#39;s own cluster instead. Behind that one line sits the machinery you&#39;ll own: SGLang and vLLM engines, B300 nodes, a shared cluster filesystem that holds every checkpoint exactly once, KV caches riding coding traffic with heavy prefix reuse, and the benchmark harness that gates every change we ship.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;em&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;edb2bdea-40e7-48f0-9485-a0bd7169c7c7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;Made by Cast AI — a Miami-headquartered, globally distributed team across 34 countries that hit unicorn status in January 2026 with a $50B+ backed investment pushing its valuation past $1 billion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Throughput. Latency. Cold starts. Cost per token.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Move those four numbers in the right direction and two things happen: customers get faster, cheaper inference, and our margins improve. That&#39;s the entire thesis of this role. Every loader you tune, every scheduler decision you land, every kernel you stare at shows up in a customer&#39;s p99 and on our P&amp;amp;L. Your mandate is the inference stack&#39;s optimization, whatever it takes, and the technical direction of how we optimize it is yours to argue with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The problem:&lt;/strong&gt; the checkpoints run 0.3-1.5 TB, and the &quot;right&quot; serving configuration depends on traffic shape, sequence-length distribution, batch dynamics, GPU SKU, memory bandwidth, and quantization tolerance, all variables that shift week to week. Most teams pick a configuration once, over-provision GPUs, and absorb the cost. We don&#39;t: we took Kimi-K3 (1.5 TB) from over an hour cold-to-serving to under twelve minutes with a shared filesystem, O_DIRECT weight loaders, and node-local JIT caches, and we&#39;re nowhere near done. Prefill/decode disaggregation and tiered KV caches are next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Python;

